  "raw": "en Español\n\n000\nABNT20 KNHC 292317\nTWOAT \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n800 PM EDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nFor the North Atlantic...Caribbean Sea and the Gulf of America:\n\nEast of the Leeward Islands (Remnants of Dolly):\nShowers and thunderstorm continue in association with the remnants \nof Tropical Storm Dolly, located about 150 miles east of the Leeward \nIslands. However, there are no signs that the system is developing a \nclosed circulation. Redevelopment of this system is unlikely while \nit moves westward to west-northwestward near 25 mph. The wave could \nbring locally heavy rains and gusty winds to portions of the Leeward \nIslands, the Virgin Islands and Puerto Rico over the next several \ndays.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...10 percent.\n\nNortheastern and North-Central Gulf of America (AL97):\nA weak low pressure area located around 125 miles south of \nPensacola, Florida is producing showers and thunderstorms. Some \nadditional slow development of this system is possible during the \nnext few days as it drifts westward across the northern Gulf.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...20 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Adams"
